% ============================================================
\chapter{Executive Summary}
% ============================================================

We benchmarked 2 Stable Diffusion models---SD 2.1 and SD 3.5 Medium---across 3 scaling modes on a single GPU (NVIDIA RTX 6000 Ada, 48\,GB VRAM). The system supports horizontal, vertical, and hybrid scaling modes. This report focuses exclusively on the generational comparison between these two models.

\textbf{Key Findings:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item SD 2.1 is 1.6$\times$ faster than SD 3.5 Medium (14.79\,s vs 23.92\,s average latency across modes).
  \item SD 3.5 Medium uses 7.5$\times$ more GPU peak memory (1072\,MB vs 142\,MB).
  \item SD 2.1 shows comparable latency across all three scaling modes (15.58\,s horizontal, 12.87\,s vertical, 15.91\,s hybrid), consistent with other v1.x-family models.
  \item Model load times: SD-2.1 at 2.75\,s; SD-3.5-Medium at 6.04\,s (average across modes).
  \item Scaling mode has negligible impact on single-worker inference latency for both models.
  \item Both models run successfully using sequential CPU offload on the RTX 6000 Ada.
\end{itemize}

